-- title:
--   A solitary minimal prime over its contraction is extended
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$, let $S$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, and let $e \colon \widehat R \to S$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion $\widehat R$ of $R$ onto $S$. Write $\varphi \colon R \to S$ for the composite of the canonical map $R \to \widehat R$ with $e$. Let $r \in R$ and $\pi \in S$ with $\pi = \varphi(r)$, and assume that the principal ideal $\pi S$ is radical. Let $P \subseteq S$ be a minimal prime of $\pi S$ (that is, a member of the minimal primes of the ideal generated by $\pi$), and assume that $P$ is the only one with its contraction: for every minimal prime $P'$ of $\pi S$, if $\varphi^{-1}(P') = \varphi^{-1}(P)$ then $P' = P$. The conclusion is that $P$ is extended from its contraction along $\varphi$, namely that the ideal of $S$ generated by $\varphi(\varphi^{-1}(P))$ equals $P$.
--
--   A statement of commutative algebra about a Noetherian local ring and its completion: under a separation hypothesis on the minimal primes of a radical principal ideal, one such prime is generated by its contraction to the base, so that $S/P$ is a quotient of $\widehat R$ by an ideal extended from $R$. It is applied in the study of Drinfeld charts on modular curves at full level, where $R$ is a local ring of the curve and $S$ a chart ring, to identify branch primes and deduce that certain stalk quotients are discrete valuation rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_map_comap_eq_of_minimalPrimes_span_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion.lean

